{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_folder_tree", "label": "Storage Layout and Folders \u2014 A Store the User Can Open", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Reverses two written decisions on the owner's explicit instruction: the blob store becomes a user-owned host directory rather than a named volume, and source files become path-addressed rather than content-addressed."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_path_addressed_store", "label": "Path-Addressed, Browsable Store", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The cost, stated plainly: identical bytes in two models are two copies on disk, and it is not recoverable by cleverness \u2014 a store cannot both be one file per model and one file per distinct content. What survives is 'hash first, always': library_holds keys on (library_id, source_path, blake3), so hashing still happens first and a re-scan still settles as Skipped. Only the filename the bytes are written under changes."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_model_directory_naming", "label": "Model Directory Naming and Slug Rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Slugify the part name and append the first six hex characters of the blake3 on collision. Directory names are cosmetic, not identity \u2014 nothing parses them \u2014 which lets the naming optimise for a human reading a file manager. Unicode is preserved, Windows-reserved characters are replaced, trailing dots and spaces are trimmed, and device names get a _ suffix, because a model legitimately called AUX is not hypothetical in a parts library."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_metadata_json", "label": "metadata.json \u2014 A Self-Describing Store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Carries enough to rebuild the rows, so deleting the database still leaves the store describing itself; there is no separate manifest directory because a manifest not beside the thing it describes goes stale. It is machine-owned and the user may delete it, so it is not defended but degraded around: a directory with no readable metadata.json is an orphan that re-adoption skips and reports."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_folder_table", "label": "folder table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_migration_0009", "label": "Migration 0009 \u2014 Folders", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_part_folder_id", "label": "part.folder_id", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_file_storage_path", "label": "file.storage_path", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Stays nullable: null means the bytes are still at the old content-addressed path, which is a live state for as long as migrate_storage takes to drain \u2014 hours on a real corpus, so a supported state rather than an edge case."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_source_path_immutable", "label": "part.source_path Never Changes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Three columns, three jobs: source_path is where the file was when we first saw it, folder_id is where the user has since put it, storage_path is where the bytes actually sit. Mutating source_path on a move means a re-scan of the original directory stops recognising the file, ingests it a second time and reports success \u2014 the silent duplication 6a exists to refuse."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_rename_then_commit", "label": "Rename First, Commit Second", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The reverse ordering leaves the database pointing at a path that does not exist, which every read then hits. A disk ahead of the database is a repair job; a database ahead of the disk is a broken grid \u2014 and metadata.json is what makes the surviving window recoverable."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_migrate_storage_job", "label": "migrate_storage Job", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "sqlx runs a migration in one transaction at startup; copying 23 GB is not that, and it needs a worker the migration cannot assume is running. It copies before it deletes, so an interrupted run has the file at both paths and never at neither."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_part_move_table", "label": "part_move Audit Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A move is not a revision: a revision is an immutable content-addressed snapshot, and a move changes no bytes, so it would produce a revision identical to its parent in every measured column and fill the version strip with zero-delta entries that are not design changes."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_source_relocator", "label": "SourceRelocator", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A third handle that can rename and nothing else. A directory rename parses nothing, reads no bytes and invokes no kernel, so routing an O(1) syscall through the job queue would honour the rule's letter against its reason and put a poll cycle between dragging a card and the card arriving. If it ever grows a method that reads or writes contents, that is the signal it has become SourceStore."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_nulls_not_distinct", "label": "nulls not distinct Folder Uniqueness", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "PostgreSQL treats NULLs as distinct in a unique constraint by default, so a plain unique constraint silently permits two root categories both named Terrain \u2014 the first thing a corpus scan produces. Verified against the project's own PostgreSQL 18.6 rather than asserted."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_folder_backfill", "label": "The 0009 Folder Tree Backfill", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The tempting claim that every pre-0009 part sits at the library root was true before slice 6a and is false after it. Skipping it strands every existing library permanently flat with no user-reachable repair, because folders are created only for files that actually ingest and a re-scan settles everything as Skipped. A level-by-level loop, not one recursive CTE, because a CTE cannot use the ids it just generated as the next level's parents."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_scan_creates_categories", "label": "The Scan Creates Categories, After the Short-Circuit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Get-or-create is insert ... on conflict do nothing then select, because two workers scanning concurrently genuinely race the same directory. Creating categories during the walk would mean a re-scan of a directory whose models have all been moved away silently re-creates the now-empty originals, on disk as well as in the database."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_soft_delete_cascade", "label": "Soft Delete Cascades Through Subcategories", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Deleting Terrain while it holds Terrain/Rocks/Cliffs must not leave Rocks alive and unreachable. Nothing is removed from disk, and the confirmation says three things: the count, that nothing is removed from the storage folder, and that it is reversible."}, {"id": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_source_dedup_lost", "label": "Source Dedup Is Gone, and ref_count Loses an Implication", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "ref_count still counts how many file rows reference a hash; what it no longer implies is one copy on disk. The consequence lands on purge: a purge that deleted 'the blob' would take another model's file."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_folder_tree", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_phase_1_slice_6a_corpus_design_slice_6a", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_path_addressed_store", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_blob_cas", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_path_addressed_store", "target": "specs_2026_09_02_phase_1_slice_1_ingest_design_hash_first_short_circuit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_path_addressed_store", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_source_dedup_lost", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_model_directory_naming", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_path_addressed_store", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_metadata_json", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_path_addressed_store", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_migration_0009", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_folder_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_migration_0009", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_part_folder_id", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-folder-tree-and-moves-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_migration_0009", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_file_storage_path", "